# Kitchen Sink / Visual Playground

Shared UI has one visual contract: the kitchen-sink playground (stand-alone host or DEV-only/debug surface — never product navigation).

## Always reuse sink elements

Product UI must reuse kitchen-sink catalogued elements, variants, and tokens. Search the catalog first (`**/kitchen-sink/`, `**/uiCatalog/`, or the project’s documented playground path). Do not invent parallel components or styles for a job the sink already covers.

## Document deviations

If product UI must diverge from a catalogued pattern, document it in the catalog entry (`doNotUse`, `whenToUse`, or `summary`) and near the call site. State why the exception exists and whether it is temporary. Undocumented one-offs are not allowed.

## Keep it updated

Any change to shared UI, tokens, or visual patterns must update the kitchen sink in the same change (metadata + live demo). Do not leave the playground stale.

## When introducing a shared building block

1. Add or update section metadata (`whenToUse`, `summary`, `variants`, `tokens`, `doNotUse`).
2. Add or update the matching section demo with live examples.
3. Ensure every `sinkAnchor` exists as a stable id in that demo; section root id matches `section.id`.
4. Register new section families in the ordered catalog (sidebar order).
5. Keep the playground non-shipping — debug/DEV entry only.

## Do / Don't

```text
✅ Always reuse catalogued sink elements / variants / tokens
✅ Document deviations (why + temporary?) in catalog + call site
✅ Update kitchen sink in the same change as shared UI
✅ Cite sinkAnchor in plans/reviews (e.g. button-variants)
❌ Parallel “primary-ish” styles beside a catalogued pattern
❌ Undocumented one-offs
❌ Shared UI change with a stale playground
❌ Ship the playground as end-user product UX
```

For bootstrap or full structure, use the `kitchen-sink` skill (`STRUCTURE.md`, `SECTIONS.md`).
